---
alwaysApply: true
---

- Before you start planning, you can have a look at the `README.md` file inside of project so you can have a brief picture of functionality it already has. It also includes links to different libraries used in project
- After finishing a task, if it's not a code review:
  - run a smoke test in a browser using playwright. Find more information inside [smoke-test-handoff.mdc](./smoke-test-handoff.mdc)
  - run unit tests with React Three Fiber Test Renderer (RTTR) via `npm run test:unit`
- After creating a new feature for the project, don't forget to document only important information about it in `README.md` file. Include only features, not bugfixes or "best practices" info. Make it concise and short.
- Git: follow Conventional Commits — `type(scope): subject` (imperative mood, no trailing period), e.g. `feat(towers): add slow tower`. The `commit-msg` hook (commitlint) and CI enforce it; never bypass hooks with `--no-verify`.
